  "id": "dominican-1550-canon",
  "title": "Dominican Missal 1550: complete Canon constituent",
  "scope": "Complete Dominican Canon constituent as the 1550 book prints it: from fol. 94r (PDF 228) Te igitur under the woodcut through fol. 95v (PDF 231) omnis honor et gloria, immediately before the heading Cantus solennis. 14 source-order units, 26 printed crosses, no rubrics printed within these bounds. The book sets the concluding Per omnia saecula saeculorum. Amen only in the following notated chant block, which is excluded with it. Whole-book and complete-Ordinary coverage remain partial; no wording is inherited from another edition.",
